capability ui/bound-values  a value a widget and the program share, which calls back when it changes
  heroes  refused: the program holds its own state and sets the widget, and a value that calls back is a closure the language does not have
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  tkinter.Variable, tkinter.StringVar, tkinter.IntVar, tkinter.DoubleVar, tkinter.BooleanVar

capability ui/styles  widgets drawn in a style the program chooses
  heroes  refused: the system draws its own widgets in its own style, which is what a native widget is; a style of the program's is drawing of its own
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  ttk.Style

dropped
  go      ui.Control, ui.ControlBase, ui.NewControlBase, ui.ControlFromLibui, ControlBase.Handle, ControlBase.LibuiControl (the interface every widget shares and the system's handle beneath it, which a program never holds here: a widget is a number); ui.LibuiFreeText, Image.Free (memory freed by hand, which the language does itself); Window.Margined, Window.SetMargined (a window's padding, `set_spacing`'s); ui.NewSearchEntry (a text field the system draws as a search field, which behaves as a text field)
  python  tkinter.Tcl, tkinter.CallWrapper, tkinter.getboolean, tkinter.Misc, tkinter.BaseWidget, tkinter.Widget, ttk.Widget, ttk.tclobjs_to_py, ttk.setup_master (Tcl's interpreter and the classes every widget inherits, which a program never names here); ttk.Sizegrip (the corner a window is resized by, which the system draws); scrolledtext.example, filedialog.test, dnd.Tester, dnd.test (the modules' own demonstrations)
